[medium] These documentation locals are never modified after initialization, so declaring them `const` (or `const auto`) would guard against accidental mutation and better convey intent.

For example:
```cpp
const FunctionDocumentation::Description description = ...;
const FunctionDocumentation documentation{...};
```

[medium] The raw string literals holding the example SQL/output start with leading indentation plus an extra newline right after R"(, which could surface as unwanted whitespace in generated docs or tests. Left-aligning the contents (or trimming via a helper) would make the rendered example match the expected formatting exactly.

```suggestion
    FunctionDocumentation::Examples examples = {
        {
            "Usage example",
            R"(SELECT
    '<tag>Hello & "World"</tag>' AS original,
    encodeXMLComponent('<tag>Hello & "World"</tag>') AS xml_encoded;)",
            R"(┌─original───────────────────┬─xml_encoded──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ <tag>Hello & "World"</tag> │ &lt;tag&gt;Hello &amp; &quot;World&quot;&lt;/tag&gt; │
└────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘)"
        }
    };
```
